# Manually aim Ball Butler (the GUI's editable Yaw/Pitch readouts).
#
# ball_butler_node forwards this to the bb/throw action with speed 0, which the
# BB firmware routes to TRACKING — the axes move, no ball leaves. TRACKING
# drops to IDLE (returning pitch to its rest angle) 5 s after the last aim, so a caller that
# wants to HOLD a pose re-sends it (the GUI renews at 1 Hz); stopping the
# re-sends is the release. Refused unless the orchestrator is IDLE and BB is
# IDLE or TRACKING, and when either angle is outside its range (nothing is
# clamped — an out-of-range request sends nothing).

float64 yaw_deg     # BB yaw frame (as bb/heartbeat reports it), within the yaw soft limits
float64 pitch_deg   # degrees from horizontal (0 = horizontal, 90 = vertical)
---
bool success
string message
